# Folders Spotlight must not index. `spotlight-exclusions apply` adds each one
# that exists on this machine to the Search Privacy list; see docs/SPOTLIGHT.md.
# One absolute or ~ path per line; a line starting with # is a comment.
#
# Folders only one machine has (its checkouts and workspaces) go in
# ~/.config/spotlight/exclusions.local, which is never tracked.
#
# Spotlight already skips hidden folders (~/.cache, ~/.cargo, ~/.claude, ...)
# and ~/Library/Caches, so only visible folders belong here.

# App-private state: Electron caches (Notion, Linear, Discord, VS Code,
# browsers), app databases, Node versions installed by fnm. None of it is a
# document; Contacts, Mail and Messages reach Spotlight through CoreSpotlight,
# not through these files.
~/Library/Application Support
~/Library/Logs

# pnpm's content-addressable store: hundreds of thousands of package files.
~/Library/pnpm

# Go toolchains from golang.org/dl, and GOPATH.
~/sdk
~/go

# TeX Live and other locally built installs.
/usr/local

# Command Line Tools SDKs and device support images.
/Library/Developer
